+\paragraph{Routing.}
+Each period is routed on the directed two-commodity core. The load commodity
+enters a served bin, the residual commodity leaves it, their sum on an arc
+equals the capacity of a used vehicle, and the copy depot closes the two
+paths:
+\begin{align}
+    \sum_{j \neq i} \bigl( f_{ij}^{t} - f_{ji}^{t} \bigr) &= q_i^{t},
+        & & i \in I_b, \label{eq:flow-load}\\
+    \sum_{j \neq i} \bigl( h_{ji}^{t} - h_{ij}^{t} \bigr) &= q_i^{t},
+        & & i \in I_b, \label{eq:flow-res}\\
+    \sum_{j \in I_b} f_{j,n+1}^{t} &= \sum_{i \in I_b} q_i^{t}, &
+    \sum_{j \in I_b} f_{0j}^{t} &= 0, \label{eq:flow-depot-load}\\
+    \sum_{j \in I_b} h_{n+1,j}^{t} &= Q k^{t} - \sum_{i \in I_b} q_i^{t}, &
+    \sum_{i \in I_b} h_{i0}^{t} &= Q k^{t}, \label{eq:flow-depot-res}\\
+    f_{ij}^{t} + h_{ij}^{t} &= Q\, x_{ij}^{t}, & & i, j \in I,\ i \neq j. \label{eq:flow-coupling}
+\end{align}
+Visited bins have one incoming and one outgoing arc, the real depot dispatches
+and receives exactly $k^{t}$ arcs, and the fleet is capped:
+\begin{align}
+    \sum_{i \neq j} x_{ij}^{t} = g_j^{t}, \qquad
+    \sum_{k \neq j} x_{jk}^{t} = g_j^{t}, & & & j \in I_b, \label{eq:degree}\\
+    \sum_{j \in I_b} x_{0j}^{t} = k^{t}, \qquad
