+
+On day~1 the myopic policy serves everyone: each bin pays its own detour
+that day, and the remote cluster is visited at light load. The horizon
+optimum declines 38.16\,€ of immediate profit and waits: by day~2 the same
+bins carry 580\,kg, the cluster pays one 21.5\,km trip instead of two, and
+on day~3 the fast bin, now forced by rule~\eqref{eq:force} at 330\,kg, is
+collected alone. The waiting trajectory records two overflow events --- the
+remote bin reaching 340\,kg on day~2 and the fast bin 330\,kg on day~3 ---
+which \eqref{eq:overflow} counts but the objective does not penalise; the
+myopic trajectory records none.
+
